    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d962">

                <pb facs="1027" n="1017" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1017"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363/6–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-24T20:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1949—8 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1287. Re ur 2438. Caltex notified with request they inform Dept of any action
                    proposed here. Nothing planned as yet. Dept on June 23 released full text Chi
                        note<anchor n="40" xml:id="d962-f1"/> re commercial shipping situation
                    Yung-chia (Wenchow), Ningpo, Shanghai, Tientsin and Chinghuangtao (Chinwangtao),
                    per Cantel 638.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d962-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d962-f1" n="40" xml:id="d962-f1-content">
